# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
As a fashion designer, I am committed to creating sustainable and environmentally-friendly clothing lines. In this revised research plan, we will incorporate new sources and updates from the existing design documents.<br>
<br>
### Objectives<br>
<br>
* Identify key factors contributing to textile waste in the fashion industry<br>
* Explore innovative materials and production methods for reduced environmental impact<br>
* Develop a framework for evaluating the sustainability of fashion products<br>
<br>
## Methodology<br>
<br>
We will conduct a literature review of recent studies on sustainable fashion, focusing on material science, production processes, and consumer behavior. We will also analyze existing design documents and research papers from the field.<br>
<br>
### Sources<br>
<br>
* [1] &quot;The True Cost&quot; documentary (2015)<br>
* [2] &quot;Fashion&#x27;s Dirty Secret&quot; article by The Guardian (2020)<br>
* [3] &quot;Sustainable Fashion: A Guide to Materials, Production, and Consumption&quot; book by Ellen MacArthur Foundation (2020)<br>
<br>
## Next Steps<br>
<br>
We will continue to research and gather data on sustainable fashion practices. We will also develop a prototype for a sustainable clothing line using innovative materials and production methods.<br>
